# FitScreen SDAD rule

- Read `docs/` before writing code. Implement one feature from `docs/04-features.md` at a time (UI + command/query + event + test).
- Commands live in `app/commands/`. They validate, append events, then project. They never return large read models for screens.
- Queries live in `app/queries/`. They only SELECT from projection tables. They never call `event_store.append`.
- Views in `app/views/` are MVC controllers: parse HTTP, call command or query, render Jinja. A view contains no SQL and never calls `EventStore.append`.
- Queries in `app/queries/` do not import `event_store` and never call `EventStore.append`.
- Never UPDATE business state on `jobs` or `applications` except inside `app/projections.py`.
- A user-facing view never writes `agent_score`. The worker records it through `complete_screening`.
- Domain is candidate screening for jobs. Do not add flights, tickets, news, or events-as-parties as product language.
- Persist CVs to `uploads/` and embeddings via `agent/rag.py` (Chroma).
- The evaluation agent runs in a separate process (`agent.worker`), not inside a Flask request.
